// Eastern Carnival: guards, citizens and Overly (Batch 22)
@1 = ~We keep the peace at the carnival. You better behave and keep your weapons away while you're here.~
@2 = ~What a wonderful Carnival. Do you know they have a real elephant straight from Chult here?~
@3 = ~I much prefer to spend my time here rather than sit at home, worrying all day about mines. To think I was considering becoming a miner.~
@4 = ~This Carnival is a great opportunity for me to leave my stressful life behind. It's cheerful, joyful and... helps me forget about all the worries that plaque the Sword Coast as of late.~
@5 = ~Amazing Carnival isn't it? Isn't it?!~
@6 = ~Ehm... yeeeaaah. Enjoy it. I'll be... over there.~
@7 = ~What is that you're holding underneath your shirt?~
@8 = ~What? Nothing. It's my skinfolds. Heh he... he...~
@9 = ~\(gulp\)~
@10 = ~(lift his shirt forcefully) This is Laslo, isn't it? A snake you kidnapped from his cage!~
@11 = ~I'm not sure if I want to see what's down there.~
@12 = ~I better go.~
@13 = ~Kidnapped?! I merely borrowed him. I started teaching him some tricks too. Look...~
@14 = ~Then do us both a favour and keep away from me.~
@15 = ~(lift his shirt forcefully) This is Laslo, isn't it? A snake you kidnapped from his cage!~
@16 = ~I better go.~
@17 = ~I said, fetch! Las... Laslo?~
@18 = ~Upon inspection you notice that the man is lying on the ground unconscious but alive. His hands are clammy, his skin pale and he clearly is unaware of his surroundings. Laslo bit his hand. Looks like provoking Dead Grass Snakes isn't the most ideal. The poison appears not to be fatal, it simply causes temporary side effects. At least... that's what you remember from the lectures you read back in Candlekeep.~
@19 = ~The man remains unconscious. Laslo is now safely in your possession, although not exactly in the most comfortable accommodation.~
@20 = ~Jaheira, is it as superficial as I hope?~
@21 = ~(Leave)~
@22 = ~Upon inspection you notice that the man is lying on the ground unconscious but alive. His hands are clammy, his skin pale and he clearly is unaware of his surroundings. Laslo bit his hand. Looks like provoking Dead Grass Snakes isn't the most ideal. The poison appears not to be fatal, it simply causes temporary side effects. At least... that's what you remember from the lectures you read back in Candlekeep.~
@23 = ~(Leave)~
@24 = ~Boo says there is no such things as moving skinfolds. Although last time I fed him a scrambled egg his tummy started turning inside out and generate strange noises. Now, that itself contradicts his theory, doesn't it? Eehm...~
@25 = ~The debilitating physical effects can last for a few days while the poison clears this idiot's system but he shall live. The venom is strong enough to kill small animals like rabbits, but humans survive the ordeal to my knowledge. He will experience nausea and muscle pain for at least a couple days.~
